          "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4BAXQU",
          "body": "yes it's `msm8916` (msm, not mdm), but the ADB shell isn't root and there doesn't seem to be an obvious way to get root. so copying the files fails, and even if that succeeds, starting the daemon will fail. `/dev/diag` is present.\r\n\r\nThe patch I had to apply to get that far was\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/installer/src/uz801.rs b/installer/src/uz801.rs\r\nindex 559635b..d32536d 100644\r\n--- a/installer/src/uz801.rs\r\n+++ b/installer/src/uz801.rs\r\n@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ async fn wait_for_adb() -> Result<ADBUSBDevice> {\r\n\r\n         // UZ801 USB vendor and product IDs.\r\n         // TODO: Research if other variants use different IDs.\r\n-        match ADBUSBDevice::new(0x05c6, 0x90b6) {\r\n+        match ADBUSBDevice::new(0x05c6, 0x9024) {\r\n             Ok(mut device) => {\r\n                 // Test ADB connection\r\n                 if test_adb_connection(&mut device).await.is_ok() {\r\n```",
          "author": {
            "login": "untitaker",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/837573?u=4b106f1ba83b3028677a861efe31c46d703e77ff&v=4",
            "url": "https://github.com/untitaker"
          },
